<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: RUGBY UNION-CORKERY AND BELL FIT TO FACE ENGLAND.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-CORKERY AND BELL FIT TO FACE ENGLAND.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish flanker David Corkery and centre Jonathan Bell will play in Saturday's Five Nations championship game against England at Lansdowne Road after reporting fit following a squad training session on Monday.</p>
<p>Corkery injured a finger playing against Wales on February 1 while Bell hurt his ribs playing for club side Northampton at the weekend.</p>
